														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3869708">
									

<p>Threat level sees only sporadic use but I rather like it, because object class doesn't always capture the true level of danger - it's more of a &quot;how easy is this to contain&quot; thing, and there are things that are easy to contain but extremely dangerous if they were ever stolen/released in a containment breach. There is a Threat Level page which tells you what each color means, so I think that it should be okay (and only by getting more use will people get an intuitive sense of what each level means - it's not like Euclid and Keter are intuitive at first glance either.)</p>
<p>For those who aren't fond of it, it's not like it replaces Object Class, which is still there. So, everyone should be happy.</p>

							</div>

								
					
