<p>To be blunt, I am rather underwhelmed.</p>
<p>The object itself is rather interesting, a window to the past that can let you see major events and confirm theories. There is potential there for interesting storytelling and experimentation. However, the test log is just various flavors of observing extinction events which are rather bland after the first few, and you expunge the one that seems like it would be the most interesting. You could have tapped into a this to offer your own take on a lot of historical phenomena and mysteries, but instead, we just get different flavors of extinction events.</p>
<p>Additionally, the tie into SCP-2000 is nothing that hasn't been explored fairly well in that very skip, and just kind of dries up the last bit of momentum the article had going for it.</p>
<p>-1. Solid concept, solid set up, didn't quite stick the landing.</p>

