														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3872752">
									

<p>Fair enough. Hopefully my next one will ring better, whenever that might be.</p>
<p>For the record, there are three reasons I don't intend to change this to something like that.</p>
<p>1) It wasn't the story I was going for with this idea. Which, okay, if it doesn't last, it doesn't last, that's how it goes sometimes. But changing it along the desired lines would essentially make it an entirely different story and thus an entirely different SCP, and I don't have a story for an entirely different SCP scripted out.</p>
<p>2) The site is already rife with &quot;oh, hey, this historical event was actually anomalous&quot; SCPs. Heaven help me if I try to actually remember all of them that have been done, lest I would step on ground that's already been trod, but beyond that, there's absolutely nothing novel about the concept, and I know how some people get when you're doing an idea that's already been done. Especially when you don't do it as well.</p>
<p>3) It requires a LOT of factors - interesting historical events that haven't been covered (as mentioned above), interesting ideas for anomalous activity that occurs during that time, ways of believably ensuring that the anomaly wasn't discovered (otherwise the Foundation would already know about them), and the ability to write this all in a way that seems both believable and compelling. Simply put, I don't think I'm up to that task.</p>

							</div>

								
