			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3907823">
									

<p>This article hinges on two things: (1) observation of extinction events, and (2) discussing that humanity has been eradicated.</p>
<p>But the extinction events aren't super interesting. It's weird to try to establish that some extinction events were caused by Generic Anomalies, and the specific details we got were underwhelming. As an example, 'What would happen if dinosaurs evolved into humanoids' has been a well-covered question outside this site, but &quot;humanoid t-rex and triceratops&quot; is both evolutionarily extremely unlikely and also was overdone already in the early 90's.</p>
<p>The discussion of humanity being previously eradicated has been done lots on this site &#8212; it's practically canon, since even before 2000. Just discussing it in a classified note is kinda 'eh', especially when the major content contributed is just to try and establish specific <em>numerical</em> details (# of times world has ended that Foundation knows about) that will be ignored outside this article in favor of more entertaining creative decisions. That still wouldn't be bad if it were being used as believable fluff to a stronger concept.</p>
<p>Consider a rework of this article post-contest.</p>

